n humans disappear, biodiversity takes a surprising turn", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03505-1?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=nature&linkId=64339141&error=cookies_not_supported&code=d1aaf870-2b26-4acc-ae60-d9cc5b33ccb0", "url": "https://t.co/RrbOSK9II8"}]}, "id": "2119410861173309773", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 43, "impression_count": 25503, "like_count": 123, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 31}, "text": "For decades, conservation has worried about the risks of too many people. In some places, it's depopulation that's the real threat\n\nhttps://t.co/RrbOSK9II8", "url": "https://x.com/Nature/status/2119410861173309773"}, {"author_id": "15862891", "created_at": "2026-11-08T10:37:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119378650017464386"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Nature - Thousands of genome sequences identify human migrations that might have spread early forms of these tongues around Europe.", "display_url": "go.nature.com/3WvQxX9", "end": 160, "expanded_url": "https://go.nature.com/3WvQxX9", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119378654840926208/z6dMUfHD?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1066}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119378654840926208/z6dMUfHD?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 137, "status": 200, "title": "Rise of Germanic and Celtic languages is written in ancient DNA", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03581-3?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=nature&linkId=64339136&error=cookies_not_supported&code=b4892cb9-cefd-466c-b421-dd602daaa8bc", "url": "https://t.co/mAHLzSRvUl"}]}, "id": "2119378650017464386", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 34, "impression_count": 20003, "like_count": 135, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 43}, "text": "A pair of studies analysing more than 4,700 ancient human genomes has identified the possible origins of Celtic 